  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "The offense couldn't carry what the pitching gave them in Cleveland.",
    "what_this_means": "Landen Roupp worked five innings on day two of this series, giving Cleveland nothing after the first. Three runs early and he still held the damage there. The bullpen followed. Hentges, Seymour, and Brubaker combined for 2.2 clean innings, four strikeouts, zero runs. That's execution. That's a game worth winning on the road. The lineup had other ideas. Five hits and thirteen strikeouts. They were chasing after the second inning and never caught up. Willy Adames drove in two with a solo shot, the only moment the bats touched anything meaningful. Three runners in scoring position across the game and zero conversions outside of that one swing. This is the inconsistency in its clearest form. The arms give them air and the bats put it right back.",
    "what_to_watch": "Boston tonight with Sonny Gray on the mound. Logan Webb's ERA sits at 1.38 over his last four starts. The kind of line that can steal a game if the offense decides to show.",
